const faqs = [
  ["What is anxiety?", "Anxiety is the body’s natural response to stress, a feeling of fear or apprehension about what’s ahead. In small doses it’s normal and even useful. But when worry becomes constant, feels out of proportion to the situation, or starts to interfere with everyday life, it may be an anxiety disorder. Anxiety disorders are the most common mental health conditions in the United States, and they take many forms, generalized anxiety, panic disorder, social anxiety, and specific phobias among them."],
  ["What are the signs of an anxiety disorder?", "Common signs include excessive, hard-to-control worry; restlessness or feeling on edge; a racing heart, shortness of breath, or chest tightness; trouble sleeping or a racing mind at night; difficulty concentrating; avoiding situations that trigger anxiety; and irritability, muscle tension, or fatigue. Anxiety shows up in the body as much as the mind, which is why physical symptoms are so common."],
  ["What is the difference between everyday stress and an anxiety disorder?", "Everyday stress is usually tied to a specific situation and eases once that situation passes. An anxiety disorder is more persistent and intense: the worry sticks around, feels disproportionate, and begins to interfere with work, school, relationships, or daily routines. If anxiety is hard to turn off, is leading you to avoid things, or is affecting your sleep and health, it’s worth an evaluation."],
  ["What treatments work for anxiety?", "Therapy such as <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/programs/counseling/\">CBT</a>, skills training like <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/treatment-methods/dbt/\">DBT</a>, and sometimes medication. More intensive care like <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/programs/intensive-outpatient-program/\">IOP</a> helps when anxiety is severe. Anxiety responds very well to treatment. At Hopewell Health Solutions, care often combines evidence-based therapy, such as CBT and exposure-based therapy, with DBT skills, mind-body techniques, and, when helpful, medication management. For anxiety that needs more than weekly support, our Intensive Outpatient Program adds structured group and individual care, and our Teen & Tween IOP supports younger clients. Most people see meaningful relief with the right combination."],
  ["When does anxiety need treatment?", "When worry or panic gets in the way of work, school, sleep or relationships, or you start avoiding things because of it. Consider reaching out when worry or fear feels constant and hard to control, when anxiety is interfering with work, school, or relationships, when you’re avoiding places or situations, or when panic attacks are happening. You don’t need to wait until it’s overwhelming, earlier support makes anxiety easier to treat. If you ever feel unsafe, call or text 988, or call 911."],
  ["What does a panic attack feel like?", "A sudden rush of fear with a racing heart, shortness of breath, dizziness or a sense of losing control, usually peaking within minutes. Get emergency care if you’re unsure whether it’s your heart."],
  ["What is a silent panic attack?", "Intense panic felt inside without obvious outward signs. Read more about <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/post/silent-panic-attacks-what-they-are-and-when-to-seek-treatment/\">silent panic attacks and when to seek treatment</a>."],
  ["Do you treat anxiety in kids and teens?", "Yes, through counseling, play therapy, medication management and our <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/programs/tween-iop/\">Tween IOP</a> and <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/programs/teen-iop/\">Teen IOP</a>."],
  ["Will I need medication?", "Not always. A <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/programs/medication-management/\">psychiatric provider</a> can talk through options with you."],
  ["Can anxiety and depression happen together?", "Yes, often. We treat <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/what-we-treat/depression/\">anxiety and depression</a> at the same time."],
  ["Can I get anxiety treatment by telehealth?", "Some services are available by telehealth; most programs are in person."],
  ["Does insurance cover anxiety treatment?", "Most commercial plans do. We <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/rates-and-insurance-coverage/\">check benefits for free</a>; we don’t accept Medicare or Medicaid."],
];
